It is late afternoon in the office.
I look at my screen.
I write the last code.
Now the task is finished.
I smile.
I close my computer.
I put it in my bag.
Then I pack my things.
I stand up.
My colleague Peter sits at his desk.
I walk over to him.
"Goodbye, Peter," I say.
"Goodbye, Maya," Peter says.
"Good evening," he says.
"Thank you, likewise," I answer.
I walk out of the office.
Out in the hallway, I take the elevator down.
Finally, I walk out of the building.
Now I go home.
